      "title": "Content",
      "content": [
        "# cFish.io WordPress Development Glossary\r",
        "\r",
        "A quick reference guide to WordPress and web development terminology used in the cFish.io project.\r",
        "\r",
        "## WordPress Core Concepts\r",
        "\r",
        "### A\r",
        "\r",
        "**Action Hook**  \r",
        "Points in WordPress code where you can insert custom functions to be executed at specific times.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Admin Bar**  \r",
        "The black bar that appears at the top of the screen when logged in.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Attachment**  \r",
        "A file uploaded to the WordPress Media Library.\r",
        "\r",
        "### B\r",
        "\r",
        "**Backend**  \r",
        "The administrative area of WordPress (wp-admin).\r",
        "\r",
        "**Block**  \r",
        "Content elements in the WordPress Block Editor (Gutenberg).\r",
        "\r",
        "**Block Editor (Gutenberg)**  \r",
        "The current WordPress content editor that uses blocks for content creation.\r",
        "\r",
        "### C\r",
        "\r",
        "**Child Theme**  \r",
        "A theme that inherits functionality and styling from another theme (the parent theme).\r",
        "\r",
        "**Constant**  \r",
        "A value defined in PHP that cannot be changed during script execution.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Custom Field**  \r",
        "Extra information saved with a post or page (also known as meta data).\r",
        "\r",
        "**Custom Post Type**  \r",
        "Content types beyond the default posts and pages.\r",
        "\r",
        "### D\r",
        "\r",
        "**Dashboard**  \r",
        "The main administration screen in WordPress.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Database**  \r",
        "Where WordPress stores all content and settings information.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Deprecated**  \r",
        "Code or functions that have been replaced with newer alternatives and will be removed in future versions.\r",
        "\r",
        "### E\r",
        "\r",
        "**Enqueue**  \r",
        "The proper way to include CSS and JavaScript files in WordPress.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Excerpt**  \r",
        "A summary or snippet of a post.\r",
        "\r",
        "### F\r",
        "\r",
        "**Filter Hook**  \r",
        "Allows you to modify data before it's used by WordPress.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Frontend**  \r",
        "The public-facing side of the website that visitors see.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Functions.php**  \r",
        "A theme file used to add features and modify WordPress behavior.\r",
        "\r",
        "### G\r",
        "\r",
        "**Global Variable**  \r",
        "Variables in WordPress that are accessible throughout the code (e.g., `$post`, `$wpdb`).\r",
        "\r",
        "### H\r",
        "\r",
        "**Hook**  \r",
        "Points in WordPress code where you can insert custom functionality (actions or filters).\r",
        "\r",
        "**htaccess**  \r",
        "A configuration file used on web servers running Apache.\r",
        "\r",
        "### I\r",
        "\r",
        "**Include**  \r",
        "PHP function to include and execute another file.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Index.php**  \r",
        "The main template file in a WordPress theme.\r",
        "\r",
        "### J\r",
        "\r",
        "**Jetpack**  \r",
        "A popular WordPress plugin suite by Automattic offering various functionality.\r",
        "\r",
        "### L\r",
        "\r",
        "**Loop**  \r",
        "The code used to display posts in WordPress themes.\r",
        "\r",
        "### M\r",
        "\r",
        "**Meta Box**  \r",
        "UI elements on the post editing screen for adding metadata.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Multisite**  \r",
        "A WordPress feature allowing multiple websites to share a single WordPress installation.\r",
        "\r",
        "### P\r",
        "\r",
        "**Parent Theme**  \r",
        "A complete theme that can be used as a foundation for a child theme.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Plugin**  \r",
        "Software that extends WordPress functionality.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Post**  \r",
        "A content type in WordPress (blog posts, articles).\r",
        "\r",
        "**Post Meta**  \r",
        "Additional data stored with a post.\r",
        "\r",
        "### Q\r",
        "\r",
        "**Query**  \r",
        "Request for specific information from the WordPress database.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Query String**  \r",
        "Part of a URL that contains data to be passed to web applications.\r",
        "\r",
        "### R\r",
        "\r",
        "**Responsive Design**  \r",
        "Design approach making web pages render well on different devices/screen sizes.\r",
        "\r",
        "**REST API**  \r",
        "Interface allowing authorized external applications to interact with WordPress.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Revision**  \r",
        "Saved versions of a post or page.\r",
        "\r",
        "### S\r",
        "\r",
        "**Shortcode**  \r",
        "Code in square brackets that adds functionality to posts and pages.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Sidebar**  \r",
        "Widget-ready areas in themes.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Slug**  \r",
        "URL-friendly version of a name, consisting of lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens.\r",
        "\r",
        "### T\r",
        "\r",
        "**Taxonomy**  \r",
        "Way to organize content in WordPress (categories, tags, etc.).\r",
        "\r",
        "**Template**  \r",
        "Files that control how WordPress content is displayed.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Theme**  \r",
        "Collection of files that determine the appearance of a WordPress site.\r",
        "\r",
        "### U\r",
        "\r",
        "**Upload Directory**  \r",
        "Folder where media files are stored (typically /wp-content/uploads/).\r",
        "\r",
        "### W\r",
        "\r",
        "**Widget**  \r",
        "Standalone blocks of content or functionality placed in widget areas.\r",
        "\r",
        "**wp-config.php**  \r",
        "Configuration file containing database connection details and other settings.\r",
        "\r",
        "**WP_Query**  \r",
        "Class used to create custom database queries.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Development & Git Terms\r",
        "\r",
        "### A\r",
        "\r",
        "**Attribute**  \r",
        "HTML code providing additional information about HTML elements.\r",
        "\r",
        "### B\r",
        "\r",
        "**Branch**  \r",
        "A separate line of development in Git.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Build**  \r",
        "Process of preparing code for deployment.\r",
        "\r",
        "### C\r",
        "\r",
        "**Commit**  \r",
        "Saving changes to a Git repository.\r",
        "\r",
        "**CSS (Cascading Style Sheets)**  \r",
        "Language used for styling HTML elements.\r",
        "\r",
        "### D\r",
        "\r",
        "**Dependency**  \r",
        "External code that your project relies on.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Development Environment**  \r",
        "Local setup for building and testing code before deployment.\r",
        "\r",
        "### F\r",
        "\r",
        "**Feature Branch**  \r",
        "Git branch created for developing a specific feature.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Fork**  \r",
        "Copy of a repository that allows experimentation without affecting the original project.\r",
        "\r",
        "### G\r",
        "\r",
        "**Git**  \r",
        "Version control system for tracking changes in files.\r",
        "\r",
        "**GitHub**  \r",
        "Web-based hosting service for Git repositories.\r",
        "\r",
        "### H\r",
        "\r",
        "**HTML (HyperText Markup Language)**  \r",
        "Standard markup language for creating web pages.\r",
        "\r",
        "### J\r",
        "\r",
        "**JavaScript**  \r",
        "Programming language that enables interactive web pages.\r",
        "\r",
        "**JSON (JavaScript Object Notation)**  \r",
        "Lightweight data interchange format.\r",
        "\r",
        "### M\r",
        "\r",
        "**Merge**  \r",
        "Combining changes from different branches in Git.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Migration**  \r",
        "Process of transferring data between systems or formats.\r",
        "\r",
        "### P\r",
        "\r",
        "**PHP**  \r",
        "Server-side scripting language WordPress is built with.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Production Environment**  \r",
        "Live website accessible to the public.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Pull Request**  \r",
        "Proposed changes to a repository submitted for review.\r",
        "\r",
        "### R\r",
        "\r",
        "**Repository**  \r",
        "Storage location for a project, containing files and revision history.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Responsive Design**  \r",
        "Approach to web design that makes pages render well on various devices.\r",
        "\r",
        "### S\r",
        "\r",
        "**Staging Environment**  \r",
        "Testing environment that mimics production for final testing.\r",
        "\r",
        "**SSH (Secure Shell)**  \r",
        "Network protocol for secure data communication.\r",
        "\r",
        "### V\r",
        "\r",
        "**Version Control**  \r",
        "System that records changes to files over time.\r",
        "\r",
        "## WordPress.com Specific Terms\r",
        "\r",
        "**WordPress.com**  \r",
        "Hosted WordPress platform by Automattic.\r",
        "\r",
        "**WordPress Studio**  \r",
        "Local development environment for WordPress.com sites.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Jetpack Backup**  \r",
        "WordPress.com service providing backup and restore functionality.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Plan**  \r",
        "Subscription level on WordPress.com determining available features.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Business Plan**  \r",
        "WordPress.com plan that allows plugin installation and theme uploads.\r",
        "\r",
        "**Custom CSS**  \r",
        "WordPress.com feature allowing CSS customization without modifying theme files."
      ]
    }
  ],
